content.text:
Also add a small alert exclamation and hp bar; already. For unalerted enemies, color ring faint.

Now CSS short landscape. Need to think carefully about all breakpoints.

Current breakpoints:
- max-width 940 turns menu to single column, hides minimap at 700 only.
- max-height 440 hides nav grid; for 844x390 this applies plus max-width 940 single column.

Let's restructure:
1. At `(max-height: 620px) and (min-width: 680px)` (landscape phones/small tablets), force two-column menu, regardless of max-width 940. Because max-width 940 rule sets 1fr; later media rule overrides if declared later. The existing max-height 560 rule is after 940, so we can add a new block after all, or modify max-height 560 to include grid. We'll add a dedicated block near the end before portrait query:

```css
@media (max-height: 560px) and (min-width: 700px) {
  .menu-screen { overflow-y: hidden; padding-top: calc(8px + safe-top); padding-bottom: calc(8px + safe-bottom); }
  .menu-main { grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr) minmax(300px, 350px); gap: 22px; padding: 4px 0; align-items: center; }
  .hero h1 { font-size: clamp(38px, 10.5vh, 60px); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .hero .tagline { font-size: 9px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .hero-actions { gap: 8px; }
  .btn-xl { min-height: 52px; }
  .btn-label { font-size: 22px; }
  .nav-grid { min-width: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 5px; }
  .nav-grid .btn { font-size: 8px; padding: 7px 8px; }
  .mission-card { max-width: none; padding: 10px 12px; }
  .card-map { height: 64px; margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .mission-card h2 { font-size: 19px; margin: 4px 0; }
  .mission-card p { display: none; }
  .card-stats { padding: 5px 0; margin-bottom: 6px; gap: 4px; }
  .card-stats span { font-size: 6px; }
  .card-stats b { font-size: 9px; }
  .btn-deploy { padding: 8px 10px; font-size: 10px; }
  .menu-footer { padding-top: 5px; }
  .operator-strip { display: none; }
  .topbar { margin-bottom: 2px; }
  .eyebrow { margin-bottom: 4px; font-size: 7px; }
}
```

Then remove `.nav-grid { display:none }` from max-height 440, or override by placing the new block after max-height440. If new block after 440 with display:grid, it wins (same specificity, later). Good. Also `.eyebrow {display:none}` at 440; new block doesn't re-show eyebrow unless set display:flex. We can set `.eyebrow { display: inline-flex; margin-bottom:4px; }` in new block, and `.tagline` maybe show. Since at 390 height, total content: topbar ~36, main flex 1 (~330), footer 20. Hero: eyebrow 12 + h1 ~ 2 lines × 42? h1 is "VANGUARD<br/>BALLISTICS" → 2 lines at font 10.5vh=41 → 74 + tagline 10 + actions (btn 52 + nav grid 2 rows × ~30 = 65) = 211. Fits in 330. Mission card: 10+? card head 12 + map 64 + h2 22 + stats 28 + deploy 30 + paddings 20 = ~186. Fits.

2. `.hud-actions` row heights fix at max-height 440:
```css
@media (max-height: 440px) {
  .hud-actions { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 42px); grid-template-rows: repeat(2, 42px); }
  ...
  .hud-toast { top: 34%; }
  .hud-objective { top: 58px; }
}
```
Actually at max-height 440, HUD objective top 62, toast default at 24%? `top: 24%` set at max-width 700 only; at 844 width, toast base top? check .hud-toast base top.

